{"commit": "226c22ab07423fd04818ddbcd3a1f594729206f8", "id": "226c22ab07423fd04818ddbcd3a1f594729206f8-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Proposal names no upstream test", "repo": "https://github.com/orlp/slotmap", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260924T002748Z-15d920e3", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/226c22ab07423fd04818ddbcd3a1f594729206f8-1/20260924T002748Z-15d920e3/origin.json": "49002a15b4f018726ba6103012816e4bb67b849dab2118d8f6175de02dcb15f3", "evidence/226c22ab07423fd04818ddbcd3a1f594729206f8-1/20260924T002748Z-15d920e3/proposal.json": "aa52ec0045f7d0f18cadb4bd33dd1ea8aeabff3e1c9ad9b28b8ec3ca88ecfd6c"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "slotmap", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Update Debug impl for KeyData to nicely format nulls. (#141)", "summary": "`KeyData::fmt` printed the raw `{idx}v{version}` pair, so the null sentinel (`idx = u32::MAX`, `version = 1`) rendered as `\"4294967295v1\"` in debug output instead of the expected `\"null\"`. The fix branches on `is_null()` and emits the `\"null\"` string for the sentinel key.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:27:48.923379+00:00"}
{"commit": "2d49bbd4fdb6c329c49ba2ac13a929198760364f", "id": "2d49bbd4fdb6c329c49ba2ac13a929198760364f-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Proposal names no upstream test", "repo": "https://github.com/orlp/slotmap", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260924T002758Z-24d46a5d", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/2d49bbd4fdb6c329c49ba2ac13a929198760364f-1/20260924T002758Z-24d46a5d/origin.json": "11d1fc9ae93eb9e0dea5d5ea050b4df4093d5d06c5346f9e395d7585919cbd1a", "evidence/2d49bbd4fdb6c329c49ba2ac13a929198760364f-1/20260924T002758Z-24d46a5d/proposal.json": "fa9bf2e9952db298b1373a93dac1642659b4c8bf53107b23e63e7dc29eac4ba9"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "slotmap", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Reject insertion of null keys into secondary maps.", "summary": "`SparseSecondaryMap::insert` accepted the null key, storing it in the backing `HashMap<u32, Slot<V>>`; subsequent queries for the null key then returned the inserted value, violating the documented \"null keys never map to anything\" invariant. The fix adds an early `if key.is_null() { return None; }` guard.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:27:58.927662+00:00"}
{"commit": "bd32b7d5ee96beef3cc3299b79ea42c340f5ad28", "id": "bd32b7d5ee96beef3cc3299b79ea42c340f5ad28-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Proposal names no upstream test", "repo": "https://github.com/orlp/slotmap", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260924T002811Z-9a55a7ce", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/bd32b7d5ee96beef3cc3299b79ea42c340f5ad28-1/20260924T002811Z-9a55a7ce/origin.json": "583c5c0d1f3f1b3d9261cb0514d07716bd366a56f86052af46cdae8e83636902", "evidence/bd32b7d5ee96beef3cc3299b79ea42c340f5ad28-1/20260924T002811Z-9a55a7ce/proposal.json": "53cac6a72e04e752f5a6a8d4528eb8e28a30205f905f37d8745ebf01e55e9ede"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "slotmap", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Fixed possible memory leak in secondary::VacantEntry::insert.", "summary": "`VacantEntry::insert` unconditionally incremented `num_elems` and `mem::forget`-ed the replaced slot, so inserting over a stale-occupied slot both leaked the previous value and double-counted it in `len()`. The fix matches on the previous slot state and only increments the counter when the slot was truly vacant.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:28:11.385162+00:00"}
{"commit": "5c3fb220071f935f77c4ef33dd4d0e745f28d2d6", "id": "5c3fb220071f935f77c4ef33dd4d0e745f28d2d6-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Proposal names no upstream test", "repo": "https://github.com/orlp/slotmap", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260924T005216Z-2ef7482e", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/5c3fb220071f935f77c4ef33dd4d0e745f28d2d6-1/20260924T005216Z-2ef7482e/origin.json": "4b421535c3e47f094e464ac8e81412dcca454a6723a8cd1dc50c9ab13811952f", "evidence/5c3fb220071f935f77c4ef33dd4d0e745f28d2d6-1/20260924T005216Z-2ef7482e/proposal.json": "6345808e78ba1f1fda360e1c160e3268958b091977533ea826480fe5cf0fa322"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "slotmap", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Fix memory leak and panic issue in clone_from. (#137)", "summary": "`SlotMap::clone_from` overwrote an Occupied destination slot with a Vacant source slot by writing a new `SlotUnion { next_free }` directly into the destination union, leaving the old `ManuallyDrop<T>` never dropped. The fix adds an explicit `(OccupiedMut, Vacant)` arm that calls `ManuallyDrop::drop` before reusing the slot.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:52:16.630914+00:00"}
